3363637736,"_gp_fcf_yield":true,"_score_fcf_yield":35.1,"_gate_int_coverage":11.622222222222222,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":55.9,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-0.06923579359895493,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":90.4,"_gate_accruals":-0.04271744724652599,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":27.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.08415222921917336,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":90.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.10500133356889135,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.010452367053954068,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":76.17602631366623,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.026906776835500995,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":42.3,"_gate_pool_share":0.20310403616296946,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.008540227876567608,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":29.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.008648909226673163,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":20.7,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.05955288408418482,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":77.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.01175696092069678,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":64.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008529020824102791,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.00043000001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.3,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"News Corporation, a media and information services company, creates and distributes authoritative and engaging content, and other products and services for consumers and businesses in the United States, Canada, Europe, Australasia, and internationally. It operates through five segments: Dow Jones, Digital Real Estate Services, Book Publishing, News Media, and Other. The company distributes news, data, and business information under The Wall Street Journal, Barron's, MarketWatch, Investor's Business Daily, Dow Jones Risk & Compliance, Dow Jones Energy, Factiva, and Dow Jones Newswires brands through various media channels, including websites, mobile apps, newspapers, newswires, newsletters, magazines, proprietary databases, live journalism, video, and podcasts. It also provides property and property-related services on its websites and mobile apps, such as realestate.com.au, realcommercial.com.au, Flatmates.com.au, and property portals, as well as residential, commercial, and share property websites; mortgage broking offering and property-related data services to the financial sector; and Realtor.com, RealPRO Select, Connections Plus, Listing Toolkit products, RealChoice Selling, and Realtor.com +. In addition, the company publishes and distributes consumer books comprising general fiction, nonfiction, and children and religious publishing through print and digital formats under the Harper, William Morrow, Mariner, HarperCollins Children's Books, Avon, Harlequin and Christian publishers, Zondervan, and Thomas Nelson; provides news and information under the The Australian, The Weekend Australian, The Daily Telegraph and The Sunday Telegraph, Herald Sun, Sunday Herald Sun, The Courier Mail, The Sunday Mail, The Advertiser, and Sunday Mail names; and operates talkSPORT, a sports radio network. News Corporation was founded in 2012 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert J. Thomson | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $9.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $416K ranks in the below the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $37K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 23\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["News Corporation is a large-cap communication services business with a $14.2B market cap on $9.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $811M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.16\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 11.6\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Communication Services ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 23% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","10 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"News Corp (NWSA) Q1 2027 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/news-corp-nwsa-q1-2027-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793901232.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"NWSA Q1 Earnings Beat on Real Estate and Publishing Gains","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024654/nwsa-q1-earnings-beat-on-real-estate-and-publishing-gains?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cearnings_article-3024654","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793895960.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"News Corp (NASDAQ:NWSA) reports Q3 CY2026 in line with expectations","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/news-corp-nasdaq-nwsa-reports-212348